this mosque in kabul was packed with  people when a bomb exploded a prominent  cleric amir mohammed kabuli was killed  in the attack so were many of his  students  it was evening prayer time and i was  attending the prayers with others when  the explosion happened it was a very  powerful blast inside the mosque many  people were martyred and wounded  some of the victims were brought to this  hospital which is run by an italian  humanitarian organization  from the blast we received in total 35  patients  two were dead on arrival one died in our  emergency room eight received the  treatment and were later on discharged  while 24 are admitted in our hospital  mainly the injures are due to the shell  and burner  outside the hospital relatives waited  for news some of them were in the mosque  when the bomb exploded they said people  were hurled through the windows by the  force of the blast  it was a huge explosion  so many people were killed and injured i  brought two injured relatives to this  hospital  the taliban says security has improved  since it took power a year ago but  several attacks have taken place at  mosques in recent months  why does it happen i think uh  with the fall of kabul into the  ends of taliban somehow  this religious conflicts have been  considered  the biggest threat to the security of  afghanistan isis  has been  proactive in  its reaction to the taliban's gains  the taliban has been cracking down on  armed groups but this latest attack is a  reminder that security remains one of  its big challenges  victoria gatenbee al jazeera
 

